1
00:01:42,170 --> 00:01:47,840
Ebisu Town

2
00:01:50,250 --> 00:01:53,220
All right, we're counting on you, good sir.

3
00:01:54,040 --> 00:01:55,880
Leave it to me.

4
00:01:57,500 --> 00:02:00,520
I will take it upon myself...

5
00:02:00,520 --> 00:02:06,440
to lay Yasuie's body to rest in Kuri.

6
00:02:19,210 --> 00:02:21,870
Please provide him with the utmost of care.

7
00:02:22,240 --> 00:02:24,290
Naturally...

8
00:02:24,780 --> 00:02:30,800
We, too, are greatly indebted to Lord Yasuie...

9
00:02:32,800 --> 00:02:36,840
We're all set! Let's get
a move on, Nami and Kanjuro!

10
00:02:37,290 --> 00:02:38,390
Okay!

11
00:02:38,390 --> 00:02:41,310
Ah, I will be right there! Let us make haste!

12
00:02:45,240 --> 00:02:48,530
Have a safe journey!

13
00:02:52,860 --> 00:02:57,320
Wano Country

14
00:02:52,860 --> 00:02:57,320
Kuri

15
00:02:52,860 --> 00:02:57,320
Kibi

16
00:02:52,860 --> 00:02:57,320
Flower
Capital

17
00:02:52,860 --> 00:02:57,320
Ringo

18
00:02:52,860 --> 00:02:57,320
Udon

19
00:02:52,860 --> 00:02:57,320
Hakumai

20
00:02:52,860 --> 00:02:57,320
Oni

21
00:02:53,530 --> 00:02:57,320
At a dock on the way from the Flower Capital to Kuri...

22
00:02:58,410 --> 00:03:04,290
To capture the vile fugitives who
made an attempt on Lord Orochi's life,

23
00:03:04,730 --> 00:03:08,670
we've set up checkpoints
all around the Flower Capital!

24
00:03:13,680 --> 00:03:15,970
All of you, show your faces!

25
00:03:16,650 --> 00:03:17,590
What should we do?

26
00:03:18,520 --> 00:03:21,720
It looks like our escape won't be so easy.

27
00:03:22,360 --> 00:03:26,060
We can't get to Kuri
if we don't get on that boat.

28
00:03:26,060 --> 00:03:29,710
We've gotta figure out a way past it.

29
00:03:45,850 --> 00:03:47,290
What?!

30
00:03:51,590 --> 00:03:56,800
A curse on you!

31
00:03:59,080 --> 00:04:02,140
Th-They're being haunted by a ghost!

32
00:04:03,050 --> 00:04:05,620
Y-You may pass!

33
00:04:09,370 --> 00:04:12,140
We got through somehow...!

34
00:04:12,750 --> 00:04:14,150
How's Otoko?

35
00:04:14,150 --> 00:04:18,280
She's all tuckered out from crying
and is fast asleep in my arms.

36
00:04:21,790 --> 00:04:26,160
I honestly don't know what to say to her...

37
00:04:26,330 --> 00:04:28,920
Daddy!

38
00:04:36,170 --> 00:04:37,760
Daddy!

39
00:04:51,730 --> 00:04:53,770
Bonekichi, give her to me.

40
00:04:53,770 --> 00:04:56,440
You don't provide enough warmth.

41
00:04:57,750 --> 00:04:58,740
How cruel!

42
00:05:07,820 --> 00:05:09,660
That's not true, is it...?

43
00:05:14,290 --> 00:05:19,260
Southwest Kuri

44
00:05:23,820 --> 00:05:26,970
Th-Those are...!

45
00:05:26,970 --> 00:05:28,020
Ships?

46
00:05:28,020 --> 00:05:28,980
Ships...

47
00:05:28,980 --> 00:05:30,940
Ships!

48
00:05:34,940 --> 00:05:38,230
I'm speechless, Ashura!

49
00:05:38,230 --> 00:05:40,610
They'll need a bit of work...

50
00:05:41,390 --> 00:05:46,580
but we salvaged them from all of
Wano's harbors that Kaido laid to waste.

51
00:05:46,930 --> 00:05:51,870
These are enough to ferry thousands
of warriors to Onigashima!

52
00:05:52,400 --> 00:05:57,290
You are quite dependable!
My opinion of you has improved!

53
00:05:57,290 --> 00:06:01,970
Yes, mine too. You were never
known to be so sensible.

54
00:06:05,720 --> 00:06:09,100
It's not as if I was asleep for twenty years!

55
00:06:09,700 --> 00:06:14,310
I will ask Master Franosuke
to service these later!

56
00:06:15,750 --> 00:06:20,190
The journey thus far
has been long and arduous,

57
00:06:23,730 --> 00:06:28,690
but now the day of the raid is within sight!

58
00:06:39,000 --> 00:06:41,510
Onigashima

59
00:06:49,900 --> 00:06:53,770
I'm sure I knocked the ship
off of the waterfall...

60
00:06:53,770 --> 00:06:57,650
King, you bastard!
Always doing things half-assed!

61
00:06:57,650 --> 00:07:01,260
Queen, Bro... Why did you bring her here?

62
00:07:01,260 --> 00:07:06,110
Shut up! We lost comms in Udon!
What was I supposed to do?!

63
00:07:08,750 --> 00:07:09,660
King!

64
00:07:10,790 --> 00:07:14,530
I'll forget what you did to me,

65
00:07:14,530 --> 00:07:16,670
if you join me.

66
00:07:22,170 --> 00:07:27,720
All kinds of people live in
my country... except for three.

67
00:07:27,720 --> 00:07:32,640
One of them seems to have dwindled
and faded into the mists of time...

68
00:07:33,150 --> 00:07:35,140
yet here you stand in the flesh.

69
00:07:35,140 --> 00:07:36,390
I refuse!

70
00:07:42,570 --> 00:07:44,400
That's too bad.

71
00:07:44,900 --> 00:07:47,710
Well, unlock these handcuffs already.

72
00:07:47,710 --> 00:07:50,870
What the hell do you mean, "Well"?!
Forget it, you old bag!

73
00:07:51,320 --> 00:07:52,820
Have you heard?

74
00:07:53,950 --> 00:07:59,420
Big Mom and Viceroy Kaido were once
part of the same pirate crew.

75
00:07:59,420 --> 00:08:04,340
What's going on here? Set her free.

76
00:08:07,520 --> 00:08:08,680
– Viceroy Kaido!
– Viceroy Kaido!

77
00:08:09,050 --> 00:08:12,390
So you finally showed your face, Linlin.

78
00:08:16,300 --> 00:08:18,020
Kaido.

79
00:08:29,440 --> 00:08:32,950
Hey, you! You were told to set me free.

80
00:08:32,950 --> 00:08:34,900
– What?!
– What?!

81
00:08:34,900 --> 00:08:37,910
No way! It had to have been a joke...

82
00:08:38,340 --> 00:08:39,460
Set her free!

83
00:08:40,010 --> 00:08:41,290
Kaido...!

84
00:08:50,460 --> 00:08:52,930
How many decades has it been...?

85
00:08:53,440 --> 00:08:54,710
Napoleon!

86
00:08:59,180 --> 00:09:00,940
Yes, Mama!

87
00:09:00,940 --> 00:09:04,060
It's so good to have you
back to your normal self!

88
00:09:04,060 --> 00:09:06,650
I'm so shy around strangers,
I couldn't do anything!

89
00:09:08,520 --> 00:09:11,410
I told you I'd kill you
if you showed your face here.

90
00:09:11,850 --> 00:09:14,950
What idiot travels this far
to her own execution?

91
00:09:56,030 --> 00:09:58,080
The
Next
Day

92
00:09:58,080 --> 00:09:59,950
Oihagi
Bridge
Ringo

93
00:10:12,810 --> 00:10:13,880
Two-Sword Style...

94
00:10:15,050 --> 00:10:17,720
Seven-Twenty-Pound Phoenix!

95
00:10:28,480 --> 00:10:30,530
I have more weapons than you!

96
00:10:38,070 --> 00:10:40,330
What's your deal, anyway?!

97
00:10:41,700 --> 00:10:43,330
Are you friend... or foe?!

98
00:10:46,310 --> 00:10:47,920
Who the hell are you?!

99
00:11:01,020 --> 00:11:06,440
Why are you ripping off weapons
from people who cross the bridge?!

100
00:11:06,910 --> 00:11:09,230
Just give me back my sword.

101
00:11:09,690 --> 00:11:13,940
Don't throw away your life
over a single blade.

102
00:11:28,940 --> 00:11:32,460
I cannot allow its return! I shall
give you any sword but that one!

103
00:11:40,700 --> 00:11:45,310
The blade you carried was Shusui,
a national treasure stolen from Wano!

104
00:11:47,440 --> 00:11:49,690
What? Shusui?!

105
00:11:49,690 --> 00:11:54,070
Our misfortune began
the moment it was taken!

106
00:11:54,960 --> 00:11:57,530
The God of the Blade grew wrathful,

107
00:11:57,980 --> 00:12:03,700
bringing defeat after defeat to each region,
until the entire country fell to the invaders!

108
00:12:08,050 --> 00:12:09,290
What's this "god" drivel?!

109
00:12:10,500 --> 00:12:12,710
Blasphemer!

110
00:12:31,200 --> 00:12:33,770
Cease your fighting!

111
00:12:50,250 --> 00:12:56,280
What could compel a samurai and a monk
to fight out in the remote countryside?

112
00:12:56,280 --> 00:13:00,180
What's most humorous is that
neither of you intend to kill the other!

113
00:13:00,990 --> 00:13:01,800
A fishman?

114
00:13:27,240 --> 00:13:29,740
Kawa... matsu...

115
00:13:30,210 --> 00:13:32,670
Kawamatsu?! Is that you?!

116
00:13:34,590 --> 00:13:36,210
How do you know my name?!

117
00:13:40,670 --> 00:13:43,340
Oni-
gashima

118
00:13:43,980 --> 00:13:46,080
When are they gonna stop fighting?!

119
00:13:46,080 --> 00:13:48,430
Should we evacuate to the mainland?!

120
00:13:48,430 --> 00:13:50,480
Listen up, men!

121
00:13:51,550 --> 00:13:54,980
What kind of idiot would run away
while the boss is fighting?!

122
00:13:54,980 --> 00:13:56,860
You buncha babies!

123
00:13:57,240 --> 00:13:59,000
Queen, when'd you get here?

124
00:13:59,000 --> 00:14:00,690
You ran away, too?!

125
00:14:02,850 --> 00:14:05,830
Th-That's not what happened...

126
00:14:09,420 --> 00:14:11,790
Anyway, any word from Udon?

127
00:14:11,790 --> 00:14:15,170
About that, the smail still isn't connecting.

128
00:14:17,090 --> 00:14:20,760
Alright! I'll go check it out!

129
00:14:20,760 --> 00:14:23,950
His Awesomeness is trying to escape! No fair!

130
00:14:23,950 --> 00:14:25,890
No, I said, "I'll go check it out!"

131
00:14:30,490 --> 00:14:32,060
Give me that!

132
00:14:31,330 --> 00:14:32,060
Ah, yes, sir!

133
00:14:34,910 --> 00:14:36,730
Yo, this is Queen!

134
00:14:36,730 --> 00:14:39,650
– All right! Queen!
– All right! Queen!

135
00:14:39,650 --> 00:14:43,820
This is Warden Babanuki in Udon.

136
00:14:43,820 --> 00:14:47,490
Right. It looks like the smails are back online.

137
00:14:47,490 --> 00:14:48,990
Yes, as of just a moment ago.

138
00:14:49,560 --> 00:14:52,080
I took a lot of men back with me.

139
00:14:52,080 --> 00:14:55,040
We can head your way if you're short-handed.

140
00:14:55,040 --> 00:14:57,780
What a cool way to look
for an excuse to leave!

141
00:14:57,780 --> 00:15:00,420
That won't be necessary for now.

142
00:14:59,670 --> 00:15:00,420
Tch!

143
00:15:00,420 --> 00:15:02,090
– Denied!
– Denied!

144
00:15:02,510 --> 00:15:05,090
Straw Hat Luffy, Captain Kid,

145
00:15:05,090 --> 00:15:08,850
and all the troublemakers
are locked in their cells.

146
00:15:09,250 --> 00:15:10,410
I see...

147
00:15:10,410 --> 00:15:12,760
So, I called to tell you all is well.

148
00:15:12,760 --> 00:15:13,980
Tell me all is wrong!

149
00:15:13,980 --> 00:15:15,690
Your Awesomeness!

150
00:15:15,690 --> 00:15:22,570
Prisoner
Mining
Camp
Udon

151
00:15:18,210 --> 00:15:20,840
Over and out.

152
00:15:22,570 --> 00:15:25,860
How was that, Master?!

153
00:15:26,250 --> 00:15:28,740
Good job! Thank you!

154
00:15:29,350 --> 00:15:30,370
You're a good boy!

155
00:15:30,370 --> 00:15:32,200
I sure am!

156
00:15:33,830 --> 00:15:35,670
What sort of sorcery is this?!

157
00:15:35,670 --> 00:15:38,760
A millet dumpling tamed the enemy!

158
00:15:40,380 --> 00:15:43,880
They seem to work on animals
and those with animal powers.

159
00:15:45,490 --> 00:15:48,090
It all went so swimmingly.

160
00:15:49,370 --> 00:15:52,070
And we have you to thank, Caribou!

161
00:15:52,070 --> 00:15:54,180
Oh, yes!

162
00:15:54,180 --> 00:15:57,060
It's all thanks to me!

163
00:15:58,060 --> 00:16:03,900
Now, the enemies outside think that thousands of
us prisoners are just sitting quietly in our cells!

164
00:16:04,350 --> 00:16:10,130
I wonder how surprised the enemy
will be on the day of the battle!

165
00:16:13,410 --> 00:16:15,450
You owe me!

166
00:16:15,450 --> 00:16:17,100
Understood!

167
00:16:17,100 --> 00:16:21,080
Terrific! We can finally
contact Kin'emon's group.

168
00:16:23,250 --> 00:16:24,960
Dr. Chopperemon!

169
00:16:25,450 --> 00:16:30,550
We swear we will repay you for this,
even if it costs us our lives!

170
00:16:30,550 --> 00:16:34,520
It's fine. It was a relatively easy virus to treat.

171
00:16:34,520 --> 00:16:37,640
Besides, a samurai's debt would be
too much of a burden for me.

172
00:16:38,100 --> 00:16:39,810
Th-Thank goodness!

173
00:16:40,850 --> 00:16:42,480
Even Luffytaro's all better...

174
00:16:42,930 --> 00:16:45,150
Let's go, you guys!

175
00:16:45,150 --> 00:16:46,860
– Yeah!
– Yeah!

176
00:16:46,860 --> 00:16:49,030
– Luffytaro!
– You're the man!

177
00:16:49,030 --> 00:16:50,990
– Let's do it!
– That's what I'm talking about!

178
00:16:50,990 --> 00:16:53,740
He seems healthy and popular again.

179
00:16:54,990 --> 00:16:58,830
Thanks to Lord Momonosuke bringing
him here, he has earned their trust!

180
00:17:00,610 --> 00:17:02,000
There's no mistaking it.

181
00:17:02,380 --> 00:17:04,460
He has not changed a bit...

182
00:17:04,460 --> 00:17:06,710
It has been so long...

183
00:17:07,260 --> 00:17:09,010
Boss Hyogoro!

184
00:17:15,720 --> 00:17:17,430
Oh, it's them!

185
00:17:18,850 --> 00:17:21,140
Omasa

186
00:17:18,850 --> 00:17:21,140
of Udon

187
00:17:18,980 --> 00:17:20,890
Omasa, the Sanguine Pen!

188
00:17:22,690 --> 00:17:25,110
Tsunagoro

189
00:17:22,690 --> 00:17:25,110
of Hakumai

190
00:17:22,890 --> 00:17:24,900
Split-Hat Tsunagoro!

191
00:17:26,730 --> 00:17:29,110
Ocho

192
00:17:26,730 --> 00:17:29,110
of Ringo

193
00:17:27,230 --> 00:17:29,030
Moonflower Ocho!

194
00:17:30,740 --> 00:17:33,120
Yatappe

195
00:17:30,740 --> 00:17:33,120
of Kibi

196
00:17:30,860 --> 00:17:33,120
Snake-Eyes Yatappe!

197
00:17:33,120 --> 00:17:37,360
The bosses from each region
were here all along!

198
00:17:37,360 --> 00:17:40,910
To think I would see the day
where I serve you once more.

199
00:17:41,230 --> 00:17:44,250
I am delighted you are all safe and sound!

200
00:17:44,250 --> 00:17:46,960
Your compliments are wasted
on the likes of us.

201
00:17:46,960 --> 00:17:50,920
Indeed, as wasteful as
a bowel movement after a bath.

202
00:17:51,320 --> 00:17:52,510
Absolutely!

203
00:17:52,510 --> 00:17:54,680
That is for sure.

204
00:17:56,520 --> 00:18:00,390
They're so weird! And gramps,
you suddenly got all boss-like with them!

205
00:18:02,310 --> 00:18:04,020
"Gramps"?!

206
00:18:04,020 --> 00:18:05,300
Oh no!

207
00:18:07,690 --> 00:18:09,480
– Tear off his nails!
– Cut off his fingers!

208
00:18:09,480 --> 00:18:10,740
Rip off his ears!

209
00:18:11,620 --> 00:18:13,790
You better straighten up, you punk!

210
00:18:13,790 --> 00:18:15,990
Which one and how many?

211
00:18:15,990 --> 00:18:17,700
– Your orders, Boss?
– Your orders, Boss?

212
00:18:17,700 --> 00:18:21,860
That's enough! I owe him my life!

213
00:18:28,460 --> 00:18:34,840
We will lose no time in scraping together
any rebels that are still hiding across the country.

214
00:18:35,170 --> 00:18:37,180
Mm-hm! I am counting on you!

215
00:18:37,180 --> 00:18:37,760
– Understood!
– Understood!

216
00:18:38,490 --> 00:18:41,850
You escaped death, young man...

217
00:18:41,850 --> 00:18:44,510
Be careful hereafter.

218
00:18:44,510 --> 00:18:46,400
Like I care, you jerks!

219
00:18:46,390 --> 00:18:50,060
Kuri

220
00:18:46,390 --> 00:18:49,600
Ringo

221
00:18:46,390 --> 00:18:49,190
Udon

222
00:18:46,390 --> 00:18:49,070
Hakumai

223
00:18:46,390 --> 00:18:50,060
Kibi

224
00:18:46,390 --> 00:18:50,060
Flower Capital

225
00:18:54,530 --> 00:18:55,820
What a surprise!

226
00:18:56,220 --> 00:19:01,040
So it seems, the man from Kuri
who made off with the blueprints...

227
00:19:01,040 --> 00:19:02,830
was you all along!

228
00:19:03,180 --> 00:19:07,330
We have been looking for these blueprints
of Kaido's mansion on Onigashima!

229
00:19:08,460 --> 00:19:12,090
Oh, but I put Sir Franosuke
through a lot of trouble...

230
00:19:12,840 --> 00:19:16,680
But now we can plan how
to invade the enemy's territory!

231
00:19:18,000 --> 00:19:20,280
You are quite amazing!

232
00:19:20,280 --> 00:19:22,970
Were you always so sensible?

233
00:19:22,970 --> 00:19:25,730
That's enough outta you, Dog!

234
00:19:31,810 --> 00:19:36,490
Is that you, Raizo? How are things?
Did you rescue Luffytaro?

235
00:19:37,150 --> 00:19:39,690
We accomplished that and so much more!

236
00:19:39,690 --> 00:19:43,540
It's a long story, but a rough estimate
of our current forces is...

237
00:19:49,500 --> 00:19:53,050
Th-Thirty-five hundred?!

238
00:19:53,050 --> 00:19:54,670
How'd we get so many?!

239
00:19:55,110 --> 00:20:00,910
Sir Luffy's safe rescued, and you
even found and freed Kawamatsu?!

240
00:20:00,910 --> 00:20:03,940
Oh, Kawamatsu had been caught as well?

241
00:20:03,940 --> 00:20:06,870
You took control of the mining camp too?!

242
00:20:07,440 --> 00:20:10,730
You accomplished far more
than rescuing Luffy!

243
00:20:11,850 --> 00:20:15,530
Here we come, Onigashima!

244
00:20:15,530 --> 00:20:17,480
– Yeah!
– Yeah!

245
00:20:17,480 --> 00:20:20,240
And there are yet warriors
who would join our ranks!

246
00:20:20,790 --> 00:20:24,700
However, I must inform you
of a lingering issue.

247
00:20:25,350 --> 00:20:28,620
Several weapons factories
are scattered throughout Wano,

248
00:20:29,030 --> 00:20:33,590
but almost all their products are
war machines meant for export!

249
00:20:33,590 --> 00:20:37,300
Samurai are more accustomed to
the use of swords and spears.

250
00:20:39,460 --> 00:20:45,430
Currently, procuring those is difficult
due to Orochi's ban on carrying weapons.

251
00:20:45,430 --> 00:20:50,850
If we cannot arm our rebel fighters,
the fight is over before it even begins!

252
00:20:51,330 --> 00:20:53,400
Right, that is understandable!

253
00:20:53,400 --> 00:20:55,620
The problem is serious indeed.

254
00:20:56,650 --> 00:20:58,070
Where can we find swords...?

255
00:21:02,860 --> 00:21:05,660
We have also made progress,
but I will fill you in later!

256
00:21:06,490 --> 00:21:08,780
I need to assess our combat readiness,

257
00:21:08,780 --> 00:21:13,960
so I'll head to Amigasa Village
and make it our base of operations.

258
00:21:13,960 --> 00:21:18,190
Raizo, tell me all about your group
when we meet again!

259
00:21:18,190 --> 00:21:19,610
Understood!

260
00:21:26,400 --> 00:21:28,200
Right, let's go!

261
00:21:33,480 --> 00:21:38,150
Bandit's
Bridge
Ringo

262
00:21:34,600 --> 00:21:36,210
I cannot believe this...

263
00:21:36,900 --> 00:21:38,150
Is it really you?!

264
00:21:39,400 --> 00:21:40,240
Kawamatsu!

265
00:21:40,730 --> 00:21:41,800
Huh?

266
00:21:49,510 --> 00:21:50,250
It cannot be...!

267
00:21:51,180 --> 00:21:53,780
Wait... are you...?

268
00:21:58,380 --> 00:21:59,590
Kawamatsu!

269
00:22:19,230 --> 00:22:22,950
What a surprise to run into you out here!

270
00:22:23,860 --> 00:22:31,890
More than anything, I am overjoyed at
seeing you alive and well, Princess Hiyori!

271
00:22:33,600 --> 00:22:39,000
That's right, she mentioned that
a kappa raised her after her parents died.

272
00:22:39,000 --> 00:22:44,130
Please forgive me for running away
out of fear back then.

273
00:22:45,800 --> 00:22:50,290
Even if it was just a scrap,
you always gave me any food you found...

274
00:22:57,260 --> 00:23:00,400
Alas, my training is incomplete...

275
00:23:05,000 --> 00:23:06,320
Kawamatsu...

276
00:23:07,370 --> 00:23:11,360
I couldn't bear watching you
waste away, year after year.

277
00:23:11,360 --> 00:23:13,660
You would survive if you were on your own...

278
00:23:14,280 --> 00:23:18,290
I was plagued by the thought of my
presence causing your death...!

279
00:23:32,840 --> 00:23:34,160
Your Highness!

280
00:23:37,080 --> 00:23:38,520
Does this mean...?

281
00:23:41,180 --> 00:23:43,030
I'm sorry, Kawamatsu.

282
00:23:43,950 --> 00:23:46,860
Unless I act, you cannot survive!

283
00:23:50,170 --> 00:23:53,830
I was so afraid... I ran away.

284
00:23:56,990 --> 00:23:58,620
"Dear Kawamatsu,

285
00:23:58,620 --> 00:24:03,420
Thank you for everything.
I'll be okay now. Hiyori."

286
00:24:03,920 --> 00:24:04,800
What?!

287
00:24:04,800 --> 00:24:07,430
P-Princess Hiyori!

288
00:24:13,720 --> 00:24:16,230
Princess Hiyori!

289
00:24:17,030 --> 00:24:20,650
Your Highness!

290
00:24:29,400 --> 00:24:30,780
Your Highness...

291
00:24:32,240 --> 00:24:33,730
She is not here either...

292
00:24:41,710 --> 00:24:44,000
Princess Hiyori!

293
00:24:53,000 --> 00:24:55,310
Where are you, Princess Hiyori?!

294
00:25:15,160 --> 00:25:17,740
Princess Hiyori...

295
00:25:27,990 --> 00:25:29,550
Princess Hiyori...

296
00:25:31,260 --> 00:25:35,680
Your Highness... Where did you go...?

297
00:25:42,620 --> 00:25:44,610
Your Highness...

298
00:25:44,610 --> 00:25:48,430
Princess Hiyori!

299
00:25:53,620 --> 00:25:57,290
I am sorry. I am truly so sorry.

300
00:25:58,270 --> 00:26:03,330
What a kind-hearted reason!
So that's what happened!

301
00:26:03,330 --> 00:26:06,510
Thanks to you, I've plumped right up!

302
00:26:17,580 --> 00:26:18,350
Who...?!

303
00:26:22,390 --> 00:26:24,600
We've come to take our revenge, Gyukimaru!

304
00:26:24,600 --> 00:26:27,820
We're done with you stealing our weapons!

305
00:26:27,820 --> 00:26:29,860
Today, we take them all back!

306
00:26:34,240 --> 00:26:38,120
You gotta be unable to move now!
This magnum's for hunting savage beasts!

307
00:26:39,580 --> 00:26:41,620
Get behind the trees, Lady Hiyori!

308
00:26:41,620 --> 00:26:42,580
Okay!

309
00:26:43,830 --> 00:26:46,010
Hm? Are they with Gyukimaru?

310
00:26:46,010 --> 00:26:48,210
Whatever. Kill 'em all!

311
00:26:50,340 --> 00:26:51,880
Die!

312
00:27:00,230 --> 00:27:01,680
Kappa Style...

313
00:27:01,680 --> 00:27:02,650
Two-Sword Style...

314
00:27:02,650 --> 00:27:03,980
River of Retribution!

315
00:27:03,980 --> 00:27:05,100
Rhino Cycle!

316
00:27:17,910 --> 00:27:19,030
Master Kawamatsu!

317
00:27:22,130 --> 00:27:23,210
Kawamatsu!

318
00:27:23,210 --> 00:27:25,500
Are you okay, Princess Hiyori?

319
00:27:27,990 --> 00:27:30,170
Master Kawamatsu...

320
00:27:33,750 --> 00:27:36,740
Hey, wait! Are you running away again?!

321
00:27:37,260 --> 00:27:40,220
Bastard! Give me back my Shusui!

322
00:27:46,460 --> 00:27:51,440
Master Kawamatsu, I'm so glad...
to see you alive and well!
